  "question": {
    "text": "<p>For two non-zero complex number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>Re</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>Re</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, then which of the following are possible?</p><p>(A) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>Im</mo><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>Im</mo><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />(B) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>Im</mo><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>Im</mo><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />(C) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>Im</mo><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>Im</mo><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />(D) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>Im</mo><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>Im</mo><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:</p>",
    "image": null
